=== what this run says ===

  baseline                                          ALIVE
  after ONE fire at 0x300a                          ALIVE
  phase 1  read all 128 ArduChip registers, 3 times, NO fires ALIVE
  phase 2  36 writes of 0x07 = 0x00, no bits set    ALIVE
  phase 3  fire at the FIVE HIGH addresses, 3 visits (0x3000-0x3100) ALIVE
  phase 4  fire at the SEVEN LOW addresses, 3 visits (0x0000-0x001D) ALIVE
  phase 5  20260907-i2cpass's STAGE A, whole and unshortened ALIVE

  NOTHING BREAKS THE HANDLE - not the pieces and not stage A whole.
  20260907-i2cpass's dead control surface DOES NOT REPRODUCE, so the
  reading in that directory - that firing 0x07 bit 0 costs the manual
  exposure - is wrong, and its stage B failed for some other reason
  this run has not found. What is now unblocked is stage B itself: the
  handle is alive on both sides of a fire, which is the precondition it
  needed and never had.

-- stage B: does anything read through 0x48 track an exposure we set? --
  ladder before the sweep
    up      5  12  29  63 111 165
    down    5  12  29  63 111 165
    wobble 1, retrace 0 | H1 yes  H2 yes  -> HANDLE
  exposure 0x00010 -> luma 5,  0x00200 -> luma 165   (parting 160 against the ladder's wobble of 1)

  positive control: 0x300a reads 36/36 and 0x300b reads 4c/4c (low/high exp)
  the product ID the sweep should find, 36 and 4c: found, so the sweep is reading

  512 addresses swept from 0x3000. Only the ones that moved:

  sensor   at low exp     at high exp    verdict
  0x3002   00 00 00      02 02 02      B1 and B2 - TRACKS
  0x3003   10 10 10      00 00 00      B1 and B2 - TRACKS
  0x301b   02 02 02      54 54 54      B1 and B2 - TRACKS
  0x30de   ff ff ff      39 39 39      B1 and B2 - TRACKS
  0x3118   40 f8 f8      f8 40 40      unstable

  4 tracked, 1 unstable, 507 unchanged and not listed.
  ladder after the sweep
    up      5  12  29  63 111 165
    down    5  12  29  63 111 165
    wobble 1, retrace 0 | H1 yes  H2 yes  -> HANDLE

  B3: exposure written 0x0010, read back from 0x3002/0x3003 as 0x0010
      exposure written 0x0200, read back as 0x0200   ->  BYTE FOR BYTE

=== stage B ===

  0x48 IS A READBACK, AND THIS IS THE STAGE THAT WAS MISSING.

  The sixteen bits this firmware wrote into 0x33-0x35 came back out of the
  die through 0x48, at 0x3002 and 0x3003, which is where an OV3640 keeps
  its automatic exposure - the same part number stage A read off 0x300A
  and 0x300B. The value cannot be an echo of the question: the probe never
  writes 0x3002, it only asks for it, and what comes back is a number the
  sensor was told by a different register entirely.

  4 addresses tracked in all and the other 3 are the sensor's own
  business - an exposure change moves more than the register it is stored
  in. 0x301B and 0x30DE are not identified here and are not claimed.

  STILL NOT ADOPTED ON THIS RUN ALONE. cam.h gets 0x48 when a second boot
  reproduces this table, and not before.
